t: space-between;\n    padding: 18px 14px 0;\n    font-size: 24px;\n  }\n  .ad-two .headline {\n    font-size: 26px;\n    margin-top: 23px;\n    letter-spacing: 1px;\n  }\n  .ad-two .copy {\n    text-align: left;\n    font-size: 19px;\n    line-height: 1.45;\n    margin-top: 25px;\n    letter-spacing: 1px;\n  }\n  .ad-two .display {\n    font-size: 25px;\n    margin-top: 18px;\n  }\n  .ad-three {\n    height: 450px;\n    margin-top: 8px;\n    padding: 26px 26px 12px;\n    font-family: Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", serif;\n  }\n  .ad-three .corp {\n    font-family: Impact, \"Arial Narrow\", sans-serif;\n    font-size: 51px;\n    letter-spacing: 1px;\n    margin-bottom: 27px;\n  }\n  .ad-three .featuring {\n    font-size: 28px;\n    font-weight: bold;\n    font-style: italic;\n    margin-bottom: 18px;\n  }\n  .ad-three .types {\n    font-size: 30px;\n    font-weight: bold;\n    margin: 15px 0;\n  }\n  .ad-three .and {\n    font-size: 26px;\n    font-style: italic;\n    font-weight: bold;\n    margin: 19px 0;\n  }\n  .ad-three .tile {\n    font-family: Georgia, serif;\n    font-size: 27px;\n    font-weight: bold;\n    letter-spacing: 9px;\n    margin: 22px 0 35px;\n  }\n  .ad-three .bottom-line {\n    display: flex;\n    justify-content: space-around;\n    font-size: 24px;\n    font-weight: bold;\n  }\n  .article h1 {\n    margin: 0 0 52px;\n    text-align: center;\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    font-size: 50px;\n    line-height: 1.65;\n    font-weight: 400;\n    letter-spacing: 1px;\n  }\n  .article p {\n    margin: 0 0 18px;\n    text-align: justify;\n    text-indent: 42px;\n    font-size: 26px;\n    line-height: 1.28;\n  }\n  .article p:first-of-type { text-indent: 0; }\n  .bottom-ad {\n    position: absolute;\n    top: 1364px;\n    left: 12px;\n    width: 1450px;\n    height: 565px;\n    border: 2px solid #777;\n    text-align: center;\n    padding: 18px 55px 10px;\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n  }\n  .bottom-ad .complete {\n    font-size: 31px;\n    font-weight: bold;\n    margin-bottom: 2px;\n  }\n  .bottom-ad .rendering {\n    font-family: Impact, \"Arial Black\", sans-serif;\n    font-size: 160px;\n    line-height: .92;\n    letter-spacing: 2px;\n    transform: scaleX(1.02);\n    margin-left: -10px;\n  }\n  .bottom-ad .service {\n    font-size: 30px;\n    font-weight: bold;\n    margin-top: 7px;\n  }\n  .bottom-ad .description {\n    width: 1110px;\n    margin: 15px auto 0;\n    text-align: justify;\n    font-size: 18px;\n    line-height: 1.3;\n    letter-spacing: 1px;\n  }\n  .bottom-ad .visit {\n    font-family: Georgia, serif;\n    font-size: 20px;\n    margin-top: 16px;\n  }\n  .bottom-ad .details {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.25fr 1fr;\n    align-items: end;\n    margin-top: 15px;\n    font-family: Georgia, serif;\n    font-size: 17px;\n    line-height: 1.25;\n  }\n  .bottom-ad .left-detail {\n    text-align: left;\n    font-style: italic;\n    padding-left: 40px;\n  }\n  .bottom-ad .middle-detail { text-align: center; }\n  .bottom-ad .right-detail {\n    text-align: right;\n    padding-right: 10px;\n    font-style: italic;\n  }\n  .footer {\n    position: absolute;\n    top: 1928px;\n    left: 0;\n    width: 1460px;\n    display: flex;\n    justify-content: space-between;\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    font-size: 22px;\n  }\n  .footer .page-number { font-family: Georgia, serif; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"page\">\n  <div class=\"upper\">\n    <div class=\"left-column\">\n      <section class=\"ad ad-one\">\n        <div class=\"company\">MONCERET &amp; BRISTER<br>APPLIANCES, INC.</div>\n        <div class=\"brands\">RCA VICTOR<br>RCA WHIRLPOOL</div>\n        <div class=\"address\">416 Lofaso &nbsp;—&nbsp; DI 8-6702 &nbsp;—&nbsp; Baton Rouge</div>\n        <div class=\"invite\">We invite you to visit Exhibit No. 26</div>\n      </section>\n\n      <section class=\"ad ad-two\">\n        <div class=\"script\">Architectural Products<br>Manufacturing Company, Inc.</div>\n        <div class=\"line-address\">\n          <span>1245 Texas Avenue</span>\n          <span>Shreveport, Louisiana</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"headline\">PRESENTS TOMORROWS PRODUCTS TODAY</div>\n        <div class=\"copy\">\n          Permanently Finished Color Coordinated Building Com-<br>\n          ponents Including Completely Factory Fabricated PERMA<br>\n          FINISH® Doors, Toilet Partitions, and Cabinetry.\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"display\">See our Display in Booth 30 and Wall Space 58</div>\n      </section>\n\n      <section class=\"ad ad-three\">\n        <div class=\"corp\">Cocreham Materials Corp.</div>\n        <div class=\"featuring\">Featuring</div>\n        <div class=\"types\">All Types of Face Brick</div>\n        <div class=\"and\">And</div>\n        <div class=\"tile\">ARKETEX GLAZED TILE</div>\n        <div class=\"bottom-line\">\n          <span>Box 442</span>\n          <span>Baton Rouge, La.</span>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n    </div>\n\n    <main class=\"right-column article\">\n      <h1>FIVE-STATE&nbsp;&nbsp; AIA<br>CONFERENCE&nbsp;&nbsp; SET</h1>\n\n      <p>Architects from the five states of Louisiana, Mississippi, Arkansas, Alabama, and Tennessee meet in Baton Rouge on November 15-18 to look at the performance of their profession in regional growth and to map out their role for the future in development of the Gulf South States.</p>\n\n      <p>Basic factors affecting development of the five states will be examined by panelists well qualified in their respective fields of politics, economics, technical factors, sociological influences, etc. The participants will attempt to chart the means by which architects can influence development with an appreciation for function, durability and beauty.</p>\n\n      <p>Panelists and speakers will include Phil Will, Jr. and Henry Wright, president and first vice-president of the American Institute of Architects, respectively; Clinton Brush III, Gulf States Regional Director; Dexter Keezer, chief economist for McGraw-Hill Publishing Company; Dudley Hunt, senior editor of Architectural Record; Buford Pickens, director of Building at Washington University in St. Louis and former dean of the Tulane School of Architecture; Edward Steimel, executive director of Louisiana’s Public Affairs Research Council; James Shilstone, partner in Shilstone Testing Laboratories.</p>\n\n      <p>Thomas Biggs, member of the National AIA Education Committee; O. J. Baker, head of the LSU Dept. of Architecture; John Williams, head of the Dept. of Architecture at the University of Arkansas; Gordon C. Wittenberg, national chairman of the AIA Public Relations Committee; George F. Pierce, chairman of the National AIA’s Chapter Affairs Committee; Wolf Von Eckardt, and Maurice Perreault, both of the National AIA Staff, and Max Fetty, partner in Fetty/Hundemer &amp; Associates, Baton Rouge public relations firm.</p>\n\n      <p>Some 60 exhibit spaces have been rented by manufacturers wherein they will exhibit building products to attending architects.</p>\n    </main>\n  </div>\n\n  <section class=\"bottom-ad\">\n    <div class=\"complete\">A COMPLETE</div>\n    <div class=\"rendering\">RENDERING</div>\n    <div class=\"service\">AND GRAPHIC ARTS SERVICE</div>\n    <div class=\"description\">\n      For the finest in Architectural Renderings, prepared skillfully and with professional quality in every detail, you are invited to make our studios your standard source. At your disposal is our full-time staff of six capable, experienced artists—the most versatile such a group now serving clients throughout the Southeastern states. You are cordially invited to visit our studios and inspect our work and facilities.\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"visit\">See our wall display located at Booth Number 60 at the convention.</div>\n    <div class=\"details\">\n      <div class=\"left-detail\">\n        Advertising &nbsp; • &nbsp; Marketing &nbsp; • &nbsp; Merchandising<br>\n        <span style=\"font-style:normal;\">FETTY/HUNDEMER &amp; ASSOCIATES</span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"middle-detail\">\n        Baton Rouge, Louisiana<br>\n        SUITE 400, UNION FEDERAL BUILDING<br>\n        500 Laurel Street\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"right-detail\">\n        Dickens 2-2681<br>\n        <span style=\"font-style:normal;\">JOHN H. SCHAEFER</span><br>\n        Executive Art Director\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <div class=\"footer\">\n    <span class=\"page-number\">6</span>\n    <span>THE LOUISIANA ARCHITECT</span>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>"
